  "construction": "Leave-one-geopolitical-zone-out cross-validation of the LGA model, T12's design with five area-level fixed effects added. Each fold drops every household in one of the six zones and refits the identical household-level binomial model: ten household design columns plus pop_density, Aridity_2020, Enhanced_Vegetation_Index_2020, Elevation and Malaria_Incidence_2020 as fixed effects (raw scale, no transform, no interaction), BYM2 on the queen-contiguity graph over all 774 LGAs built once from the full boundary file, IID cluster effect, INLA 25.10.19 defaults. The five area-level covariates are REBUILT INSIDE EVERY FOLD by T14's build_lga_covariates() with that fold's zone clusters excluded (inverse-distance weighting over the 3 nearest remaining clusters, great-circle distance, floor 0.001 km), so a held-out region's own clusters contribute nothing to its covariates; the script asserts that no rebuilt nearest-3 set contains an excluded cluster and that the builder reproduces T14's shipped table to 1e-9. Prediction rows sit at each LGA's mean household covariate profile (taken from the FULL file, as in T12, so household covariates are held known) with cluster index NA, and cluster counts and the observed/unobserved split come from cluster_lga_fixed.csv (654 LGAs with at least one cluster, 120 with none, 1,380 clusters). theta_s is the LGA prevalence with the cluster effect marginalised by the same 7-point Gauss-Hermite rule as scripts/lga_model.R; 95% intervals come from the marginal posterior of the linear predictor mapped through that integral on a 2001-point standard-normal probability grid, no Monte Carlo draws. The truth is the direct unweighted proportion from the held-out households of each LGA with a cluster-robust ratio linearisation (strata = state, PSU = cluster), single-cluster LGAs imputed the fold's median design effect. z = (model_mean - direct) / sqrt(model_var + design_var). Pass rule fixed before any fold was fitted and identical to T12: mean(z) in [-0.15, 0.15], sd(z) in [0.85, 1.15], share |z| <= 1.96 in [0.90, 0.98], pooled over the 654 LGAs that hold at least one cluster. State and zone coverage treat LGAs as independent, which understates the aggregate interval. Count-functional calibration is NOT tested: it needs joint draws per fold.",
