    "note": "Read from the shipped PDF, not from a variable name: a HIGHER Aridity_2020 means WETTER. The same page also says 'If the aridity index becomes higher than normal in a region, the climate tends to suffer from drought', which refers to a deviation above normal, not to the level, and is contradicted by the units line and by the P/PET definition; the units line governs. Independent empirical check on the 774 LGA values: r(Aridity_2020, Precipitation_2020) = +0.985 and r(Aridity_2020, Elevation) = -0.623 in T14's correlation matrix, both only possible if a higher index is wetter. So the reported r = -0.458 with severe food insecurity is 'wetter LGA, less severe food insecurity', the expected direction, not a misread sign."
